/ The flash messages left once the page has rendered, as toasts at the top
/ right. A form page that keeps its messages renders "alerts" itself, which
/ takes them out of the flash first (the login, the choice of a course).
/
/ The anchor is sticky and of zero height: at the top of the page it sits
/ right below the navigation bar, however tall that is, and scrolled down it
/ sticks to the top of the window. The toasts hang from it and move nothing.
#admin-toasts.d-print-none
  .toast-container
    - flash.each do |type, message|
      - flash.delete(type)
      - next unless message.is_a?(String)
      - color = admin_toast_color(type)
      - sticky = admin_toast_sticky?(type)
      / An id of its own: a refresh morphs the page, and without it the toast of
      / an earlier message would be reused for this one, its timing included.
      / It slides in by CSS (animate.css, left out under reduced motion): Bootstrap's
      / fade is off, see the toast controller.
      .toast.show(
        id="admin-toast-#{SecureRandom.alphanumeric(12)}"
        class="bg-#{color}-subtle text-#{color}-emphasis border-#{color}-subtle animate__animated animate__fadeInRight animate__faster"
        role=(sticky ? "alert" : "status")
        aria-live=(sticky ? "assertive" : "polite")
        aria-atomic="true"
        data-controller="toast"
        data-bs-autohide=(!sticky).to_s
        data-bs-delay="5000"
      )
        .d-flex
          .toast-body == message
          button.btn-close.me-2.m-auto(type="button" data-bs-dismiss="toast" aria-label="Schließen")
